  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"0.26.3\"\n\npackage:\n  name: all-smi\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/lablup/all-smi/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 1feeb5f4d10489858220ce051b5685338063f0ad0b2588d8375bbc51516c62d8\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  script:\n    content:\n      - if: unix\n        then:\n          - cargo auditable install --locked --no-track --bin all-smi --root ${{ PREFIX }} --path .\n        else:\n          - cargo auditable install --locked --no-track --bin all-smi --root %LIBRARY_PREFIX% --path .\n      - cargo-bundle-licenses --format yaml --output ./THIRDPARTY.yml\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('rust') }}\n    - cargo-bundle-licenses\n    - cargo-auditable\n    # aws-lc-sys, pulled in via rustls/russh, builds its C sources with cmake\n    - cmake\n    - if: unix\n      then: make\n    - if: win\n      then: nasm\n    # tonic-prost-build compiles the TPU gRPC client, Linux targets only\n    - if: linux\n      then: libprotobuf\n\ntests:\n  - script:\n      - all-smi --help\n      - all-smi --version\n  - package_contents:\n      bin:\n        - all-smi\n      strict: true\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/lablup/all-smi\n  summary: Command-line utility for monitoring GPU hardware\n  description: |\n    all-smi is a command-line utility for monitoring GPU and NPU hardware\n    across multiple systems. It provides a real-time view of accelerator\n    utilization, memory usage, temperature, power consumption, and other\n    metrics, and is designed to be a cross-platform alternative to\n    nvidia-smi with support for NVIDIA GPUs, AMD GPUs, NVIDIA Jetson\n    platforms, Apple Silicon GPUs, Intel GPUs, Intel Gaudi NPUs, Google\n    Cloud TPUs, Tenstorrent NPUs, Rebellions NPUs and Furiosa NPUs.\n\n    The application presents a terminal-based user interface with cluster\n    overview and interactive sorting, for both local and remote monitoring,\n    and can also export Prometheus metrics via its API mode.\n  license: Apache-2.0\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - THIRDPARTY.yml\n  repository: https://github.com/lablup/all-smi\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - pavelzw\n",
